Cargohold now needs access to PostgreSQL (Backup API). Its helm values require `postgresql`, `postgresqlPool` and optionally `postgresqlPassword` (secret `pgPassword`), as well as a `galley` endpoint (set by the chart). The tables are created by brig's `migrate-postgres` (cargohold does not run migrations). Make sure the S3 prefix `backups/` has no lifecycle rules that expire or transition objects (a rule that only aborts incomplete multipart uploads, `AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload`, is allowed). Such a rule is recommended (e.g. after 1 day): timed out backup uploads are not aborted, their uploaded parts otherwise stay in S3.
Backup deletion removes all object versions and delete markers on versioned S3 buckets. The S3 credentials of cargohold additionally need `s3:GetBucketVersioning`, `s3:ListBucketVersions`, `s3:ListBucket` and `s3:DeleteObjectVersion`.
Without these permissions backup deletion stops working: a 403 on `GetBucketVersioning` falls back to listing versions, a 403 on `ListBucketVersions` leaves the files undeleted (the rows stay and the cleanup job retries).
